        {
          "id": 1021529447,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "How come this is not a 1:1 replacement?! Please recognize that there is only one column (i.e. column 0) and the sorting order is hardcoded to Qt::AscendingOrder (i.e. there is no way for user to change it)\n\nBefore this change the widget is only usable after `ui->fieldTreeWidget->sortByColumn(0, Qt::AscendingOrder);` is called. This change basically eliminates the need to call `sortByColumn` by inserting already sorted elements.",
